{"version":1,"ops":[{"type":3,"author":{"id":"bfb0c87a087f143d5d4fb3c3b303347e581f98d0"},"timestamp":1486690340,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDI3ODgzMjA3NQ==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/1259#issuecomment-278832075"},"message":"git annex git-annex_6.20170209+gitg16be7b5cc uploaded to neurodebian and includes ability to specify uuid.  Some other words of wisdom from joey:\n```\nYou can certainly pick a UUID and reuse it. A good way would be to                                              \nmake a V5 UUID, using eg the URL namespace.                                                                     \n                                                                                                                \njoey@darkstar:~\u003eghci                                                                                            \nGHCi, version 8.0.1: http://www.haskell.org/ghc/  :? for help                                                   \nLoaded GHCi configuration from /home/joey/.etc/.ghci                                                            \nghci\u003e import Data.UUID.V5                                                                                       \nghci\u003e :set -XOverloadedStrings                                                                                  \nghci\u003e generateNamed namespaceURL (Data.ByteString.unpack \"http://datalad.org/\")                                 \n93f2ac9c-94ca-5e6e-9f8c-ed49ed91b33e                                                                            \n                                                                                                                \nSince 93f2ac9c-94ca-5e6e-9f8c-ed49ed91b33e can only be generated by someone                                     \nusing the datalad url, it's \"yours\". Of course, you can use this method                                         \nto generate an many reusable UUIDs as you need.    \n```\nso indeed we